/-!
# Base change of Eisenstein extensions and preservation of lower ramification

Let `R → R'` be a homomorphism of discrete valuation rings under which `maximalIdeal R` generates
`maximalIdeal R'`, such as the residue-field enlargement `R → CompletedResidueExtension R L` of
*ÉGA III*, Chap. 0, 10.3.1. Because every uniformizer of `R` remains a uniformizer of `R'`, the
normalized additive valuation is preserved on `R`
(`TauCeti.IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal_algebraMap_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq`), and every polynomial
`f : R[X]` that is Eisenstein at `maximalIdeal R` remains Eisenstein at `maximalIdeal R'` over `R'`
(`Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.map_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq`).

When a domain `B` with injective structure map from `R` (`FaithfulSMul R B`) is generated over `R`
by a root `x` of an Eisenstein polynomial `f`, scaling `f` by the inverse of its unit leading
coefficient gives a monic polynomial `g` of the same degree, and the power-basis valuation formula
(`Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.addVal_aeval_of_natDegree_lt`) determines `addVal B (aeval x p)` solely
from the valuations in `R` of the coefficients of `p %ₘ g`. Consequently:

* `AdjoinRoot f ≃ₐ[R] B` (`Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.adjoinRootAlgEquiv`), and for any domain `B'`
  with injective structure map from `R'` (`FaithfulSMul R' B'`) generated over `R'` by a root `x'`
  of `f.map (algebraMap R R')`, the induced `R`-algebra homomorphism `B →ₐ[R] B'` sending `x ↦ x'`
  preserves normalized additive valuations (`addVal B' (j b) = addVal B b`).
* Any group homomorphism `ρ : H →* H'` intertwining actions on `B` and `B'` on the Eisenstein
  generator preserves normalized displacement valuations `addVal (σ • x - x)`, Serre's lower index
  `lowerIndex`, and the integer- and real-indexed lower ramification filtrations `ramificationGroup`
  and `ramificationGroupReal`.
* At the fraction-field level `K = Frac R`, `K' = Frac R'`, `f.map (algebraMap R K')` is
  irreducible over `K'`, and in any field extension `E' / K'` generated by a root `α` of
  `f.map (algebraMap R R')`, `E'` has degree `deg f` over `K'` and the integral closure of `R'` in
  `E'` is `R'[α]`, which is a discrete valuation ring.
* When `E / K` is a Galois extension whose integral closure `integralClosure R E` is generated over
  `R` by a root `x` of `f`, `E' / K'` is also Galois and there is a canonical group isomorphism
  `galMulEquiv : (E ≃ₐ[K] E) ≃* (E' ≃ₐ[K'] E')` preserving `addVal (σ • x - x)`, `lowerIndex`,
  `ramificationGroup`, `ramificationGroupReal`, and their cardinalities.

## Main definitions and results

* `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.liftAlgHom`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.addVal_aeval_map_eq`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.addVal_liftAlgHom`, and
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.liftAlgHom_injective`: canonical `R`-algebra map `B →ₐ[R] B'`
  sending `x ↦ x'`, valuation preservation, and injectivity under a DVR homomorphism with
  `(maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R R') = maximalIdeal R'` (ramification index one).
* `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.lowerIndex_eq`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.comap_ramificationGroup`, and
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.comap_ramificationGroupReal`: preservation of lower indices and lower
  ramification groups under equivariant Eisenstein base change.
* `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.liftedRoot`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.aeval_liftedRoot_eq_zero`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.finrank_eq_natDegree_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq`, and
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.irreducible_map_fractionRing_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq`: lifting a root
  of `f.map (algebraMap R R')` into `integralClosure R' E'`, degree `[E' : K'] = deg f`, and
  irreducibility over `K' = Frac R'`.
* `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.galHom`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.galHom_apply_gen`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.galHom_smul_gen`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.galHom_injective`, and
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.lowerIndex_galHom`: base-change homomorphism
  `(E ≃ₐ[K] E) →* (E' ≃ₐ[K'] E')`, generator action, injectivity for algebraic `E / K`, and
  lower-index preservation.
* `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.isGalois_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.galMulEquiv`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.map_ramificationGroup_galMulEquiv`, and
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.card_ramificationGroupReal_eq`: Galois preservation, isomorphism of
  Galois groups, and preservation of the lower ramification filtration and its cardinalities.

## References

* A. Grothendieck and J. Dieudonné, *Éléments de géométrie algébrique III*, Chapitre 0,
  Proposition 10.3.1.
* [J.-P. Serre, *Corps Locaux*][serre1968], Chapter I, §6 and Chapter IV, §1, Proposition 1.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open IsLocalRing Polynomial IntermediateField
